# ca-trust-ops: the regex layer flags every `-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE-----` line. A certificate is
# public by design (no private key material); these are public CA fixtures and the awk/printf
# lines that split or fake PEM blocks. Scoping the pattern to private keys is an open proposal.
# reason: prose describing the PEM fixtures; no certificate or key material
skills/ca-trust-ops/AGENTS.md:^  material\. They still contain `-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE-----` lines, which secret scanners$
# reason: awk that extracts certificate blocks from a chain; no literal value
skills/ca-trust-ops/scripts/check-ca-trust.sh:^  leaf=\$\(printf '%s\\n' "\$chain" \| awk '/-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE-----/ \{ on = 1 \} on \{ print \} /-----END CERTIFICATE-----/ \{ exit \}'\)$
